        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="d256-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve03/d256-2"/>

                <head>257. Telegram 45319 From the Department of State to All Posts<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d257-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d257-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1976-02-25T16:27:00+00:00">February 25, 1976, 1627Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <note rend="inline">[<hi rendition="#italic">Document not declassified in time for
                        publication</hi>]</note>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Foreign Policy Files, 045319.
                    Unclassified; Priority. Drafted by Palmer; cleared in AID/PPC,
                        AID/GC, S/P, PM, EA, AF, NEA, EUR, ARA, T, L/HR, D/HA, H, L/PM, PM/SAS, EB/IFD/ODF, IO/UNP, and L; and
                    approved by Ingersoll. Repeated for
                    information to Geneva USUN, SECDEF, USCINCEUR, CINCLANT, USCINCSO, CINCPAC.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="2" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>The telegram informed posts of the importance placed on country human rights
                    reports and issued additional instructions concerning submission of 1976
                    reports.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
